    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361-a1">

                <pb facs="0831" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg735"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 838.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr.
                            Avila.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 21,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith, for the information of
                    your honor’s government, a copy of a communication, with its accompaniments,
                    from the consul of the United States at Guaymas, containing information of
                    robberies recently committed by Mexican outlaws in Arizona, and that the
                    criminals habitually take refuge with their plunder in Mexican territory, in the
                    State of Sonora.</p>
                <p>I trust your honor’s government will see the necessity of adopting vigorous
                    measures for the punishment of the criminals and the prevention of similar
                    depredations in the future.</p>
                <p>With sentiments of the highest esteem, I am your honor’s obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
